  means a polarity toward atom (or group) A.

. Araki angles are associated with maximum overlap on
  the two centres (or groups). Thus angles close to 0
  have large overlap and are highly 'covalent' bonds,
  while angles near 90 represent highly 'ionic' bonds.
  They are not the angles formed in the dial diagram!

